iratory tract symptoms (catarrhal stage) and can progress to severe paroxysms of cough\n(paroxysmal stage), often with a characteristic inspiratory whoop, followed by vomiting. Fever is usually absent or minimal.\nSymptoms gradually resolve (convalescent stage). The paroxysmal cough and inspiratory whoop may be absent, particularly in\ninfants less than 6 months of age and in adults. Mild illness is common, particularly in immunized individuals. The cough may\npersist for up to 3 months.\n\nThe indications for hospitalization/pediatric consultation include the following:\n\ne Infants less than 6 months of age\ne Any child who has had apnea, cyanosis, pneumonia, or encephalopathy as a complication of pertussis.\n\nWith cyanosis following the attacks of cough, this child needs to be admitted to the hospital as the most important next step in\nmanagement.\n\n(Option A) Nasopharyngeal aspirate can be considered later, if indicated, after the child is admitted to the hospital.\n\n(Option B) Immunization, at a later date, should be encouraged even if the child has had pertussis, but this step is not a part of\nacute management plan.\n\n(Option C) Antibiotics should be considered if:\n\ne The patient is diagnosed in catarrhal or early paroxysmal phase (may reduce severity)\ne Cough for less than 14 days (may reduce spread - reduces school exclusion period)\n\ne Admitted to hospital\n\ne There are complications (pneumonia, cyanosis, apnea)\n\nAntibiotics of choice are azithromycin or clarithromycin. They can be used after the child is admitted to the hospital.\n(Option D) Salbutamol or other bronchodilators has not been shown to be helpful in management of patients with pertussis.","source_answer_status":"present","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"high","currentness_keywords":["age","antibiotic","immuniz","management","therapy"],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"ed6573075dc24a5d4959fdca1c122efb66120df7","duplicate_group_id":"exact-ed6573075dc2","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"fc7c608464044e944c57","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Pediatric amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Pediatric amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":108,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"6a0598c81a911be06dec","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 PAEDIATRIC (3).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 PAEDIATRIC (3).pdf","source_page":135,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"545553cafb9f9ae76180","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 PAEDIATRIC (3).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 PAEDIATRIC (3).pdf","source_page":136,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"854c6280732c269d8be2","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":1293,"source_qid":null}]}',1,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answer,source_explanation=excluded.source_explanation,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,visual_asset=excluded.visual_asset,visual_url=excluded.visual_url,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,currentness_risk=excluded.currentness_risk,record_json=excluded.record_json,active_quiz=excluded.active_quiz,import_version=excluded.import_version,imported_at=excluded.imported_at;
