e <3 doses pertussis vaccine; OR

¢ There is a household member aged <6 months; OR

¢ Children who attend childcare in same room as infant <6 months

Adults (regardless of immunization status)

¢ Expectant parents in last month of pregnancy; OR

¢ Health care worker in maternity hospital or newborn nursery; OR
¢ Childcare worker in close contact with infants <6 months; OR

¢ Household member aged <6 months

In the given scenario, there is no other child less than 6 months in the house other than Paul who is the index case, and none of the parents are in close contacts
with other children younger 6 than months, no prophylactic antibiotic is required; however, it is recommended that close contacts that are not up-to-date with their
pertussis immunization should be given DTPa or dTpa as soon after exposure as possible. dTpa should be considered for adults who have not had pertussis-
containing vaccine in the last 10 years.

(Option B) Parents do not fulfill criteria to receive prophylactic antibiotics.
(Option C) Parents have received their 3 doses in childhood and do not need to have it repeated again. All they need is a booster dose of pertussis vaccine.
(Option D) Nasopharyngeal swab results do not affect the management of close contacts in terms of prophylaxis; therefore, not indicated.

(Option E) Immunoglobulin (passive immunity) is not effective in reducing the chance of catching pertussis.',NULL,'Retain the source-era answer for question-bank study; verify current Australian guidance before clinical use.',NULL,NULL,'2025','v2.9.4',1,'text','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Pediatric amedex 2025.pdf","supporting_pages":[126],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-bdcd552c2cca","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"a64bbe9c478ea2343c34","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Pediatric amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Pediatric amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":126,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"ef382df2b16a0e84c317","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 PAEDIATRIC (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 PAEDIATRIC (1).pdf","source_page":45,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"60fcb25bc575736e6b89","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 PAEDIATRIC (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 PAEDIATRIC (1).pdf","source_page":46,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"97d4cb713dbd23a0b791","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":1295,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET source_id=excluded.source_id,source_question_no=excluded.source_question_no,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,system=excluded.system,topic=excluded.topic,clinical_task=excluded.clinical_task,stem_en=excluded.stem_en,answer_key=excluded.answer_key,source_explanation_en=excluded.source_explanation_en,memory_rule_en=excluded.memory_rule_en,image_ref=excluded.image_ref,source_year=excluded.s