> Back to MCQs MCQs My Exams
Question ID 1178
Title Management of sleep disturbances in a 35-year-old man on fluoxetine
Category Psychiatry / Drus & Alcohol Abuse > Normal sleep and sleep disorders
O Flag as important
Michael, 35 years old, has recently been started on fluoxetine for treatment of major
depression, diagnosed based on findings of low mood, decreased sleep and appetite and loss
of concentration. Today, he has presented because, even though his depressive symptoms
have satisfactorily improved with treatment, he has been experiencing terrifying sleep
disturbances. He explains that he wakes up in the middle of the night and sees scary black
figures around his bed. He wants to get off the bed but is unable to do so. He cannot even
move a finger, shout or call for help. The whole experience is so frightening that he is afraid of
going to sleep at all. He does not have such a problem while awake. Which one of the
following is the most appropriate management for him?','{"A":"Reassure that this is normal and resolves with time.","B":"Add an antipsychotic medication.","C":"Advise that he uses a sleep mask during sleep.","D":"Switch to another antidepressant.","E":"Advise sleep hygiene and routine."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Psychiatry  Amedex 2025.pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-ced0c344bab0","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"6c0bc68878d1d88b1a2d","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Psychiatry  Amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Psychiatry  Amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":69,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high','{"record_id":"6c0bc68878d1d88b1a2d","source_file":"Psychiatry  Amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Psychiatry  Amedex 2025.pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":69,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Mental Health","stem":"10:55PM SunSep1\n> Back to MCQs MCQs My Exams\nQuestion ID 1178\nTitle Management of sleep disturbances in a 35-year-old man on fluoxetine\nCategory Psychiatry / Drus & Alcohol Abuse > Normal sleep and sleep disorders\nO Flag as important\nMichael, 35 years old, has recently been started on fluoxetine for treatment of major\ndepression, diagnosed based on findings of low mood, decreased sleep and appetite and loss\nof concentration. Today, he has presented because, even though his depressive symptoms\nhave satisfactorily improved with treatment, he has been experiencing terrifying sleep\ndisturbances. He explains that he wakes up in the middle of the night and sees scary black\nfigures around his bed. He wants to get off the bed but is unable to do so. He cannot even\n