Question ID 1169
Title identifying the behavioral problem in a 23-year-old woman requesting a medical certificate
Category Psychiatry / Drus & Alcohol Abuse > Personality disorders
() Flag as important
A 23-year-old woman presents to your clinic asking for a medical certificate for her employer,
clarifying that you had visited her in the practice for her issue. She says she was not able to go
to work for the past two days because she had diarrhea and a fever. You explain that you
cannot do that because she has never been your patient and you cannot make a false
statement. Upon your refusal, she becomes irritated and starts shouting at you and
threatening you. You check the clinic records and realize that she was previously treated for a
