Accompanied by his wife, a 63-year-old man presents to your practice for consultation. She is
concerned about his husband because he has recently behaved childishly and bizarrely. Last
week, he was dismissed from his job as a manager in a local restaurant because he was rude
to customers and shouted at his colleagues. He does not shave, bathe or change his clothes
