Question ID 942
Title Diagnosing the cause of an abnormal behavioral patterns in a 33-year-old woman
Category Psychiatry / Drus & Alcohol Abuse > Personality disorders
(CD Flag as important
A nurse calls you to see a 33-year-old woman who has just been admitted to the general ward and
is making trouble by arguing with the nursing staff. When you step into her room and she sees you,
she says seductively: ‘Oh, my lovely doctor. | am sure you are a gentleman and understand my
needs. | want a private room with classy and beautiful furniture, | can''t eat hospital foods because
they are rubbish. | need to order French dishes as they are my favourite. | need access to my
makeup artist and want my little dog here for comfort. | am sure you are brilliant and know what |
am talking about. You are the one who understands me. These idiot nurses don''t’. Which of the
